Upload symbol files (React Native sourcemaps, Android R8/ProGuard mappings, or Apple dSYMs) to LaunchDarkly for error monitoring

Usage:
  ldcli symbols upload [flags]

Required flags:
      --project string   The project key
      --type string      The symbol type to upload (supported:
                         react-native, android, apple-dsym, flutter;
                         apple-dsym also accepts
                         ios/ipados/tvos/watchos/visionos/macos/apple/dsym; flutter also accepts dart)

Optional flags:
      --app-version string   The current version of your deploy. With
                             --type android this is read from the packaged
                             build when omitted
      --backend-url string   An optional backend url for self-hosted
                             deployments. Defaults to the observability
                             API of whichever instance --base-uri names
                             (https://pri.observability.app.launchdarkly.com for the default)
      --base-path string     An optional base path for the uploaded symbol
                             files
      --include-sources      Also upload your source files so the errors
                             page can show source context around native
                             frames (apple-dsym and android). Your source
                             is stored in LaunchDarkly
      --no-skip-existing     Re-upload symbols even when LaunchDarkly
                             already has them. By default a symbols-id
                             file that is already stored is skipped, since
                             its id is derived from its contents
      --path string          Sets the directory of where the symbol files
                             are. With --type android, run from your
                             project root and the R8 mapping is found for
                             you; with --type apple-dsym, an Xcode build
                             phase uploads what it just built (default ".")
      --source-path string   Directory to scan for .java/.kt sources when
                             using --include-sources with --type android
                             (default ".")
      --symbols-id string    The symbols id
                             (launchdarkly.symbols_id.htlhash) to key
                             uploads by (Symbols Id Lane). If omitted, a
                             *.symbolsid sidecar next to the bundle is
                             used when present, and with --type android
                             the id the packaged app reports, or failing
                             that the one R8 recorded in the mapping

Global flags:
  -h, --help                  Get help about any command
      --access-token string   LaunchDarkly access token with write-level access
      --analytics-opt-out     Opt out of analytics tracking
      --base-uri string       LaunchDarkly base URI (default "https://app.launchdarkly.com")
      --fields strings        Comma-separated list of top-level fields to include in JSON output (e.g., --fields key,name,kind)
      --json                  Output JSON format (shorthand for --output json)
  -o, --output string         Output format: json, plaintext, or markdown (default: plaintext in a terminal, json otherwise) (default "json")
